    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2HLw2z8VjshZvqFkEUXdGxs)_\n\n## Summary\n- Adds `sp-author-notes-works-dryrun` (preview, writes nothing) and `sp-author-notes-works-convert` (writes), named per ADR 0025, for the author note in the current buffer.\n- Formatting is reused, not duplicated: the lint's `sp-author-notes--person-pass` and `sp-author-notes-works-spec`.\n- **Edited works:** a second table under an `Edited works` heading lists works whose `pub-editor` links to the person and whose `pub-author` does not (`sp-author-notes-edited-spec`). New spec key `:except-prop` in the query tables makes that exclusion.\n- **Lint:** `sp-author-notes` adds the `Edited works` heading and table only to a person linked under `pub-editor` in some litnote (a mistyped key counts). Everyone else gets the `Works` table alone.\n- **Works commands:** add the second table only when the database has a work the person only edited.\n- **BibTeX:** `sp-author-notes-bibtex` reads `editor` fields (editor-only entries too) and links a litnote with `pub-editor` when the person only edited the entry.\n- Docs (bullet lists) in `docs/tangles/funct/sp-org-lint.org` and the query-tables doc; tests added; no CHANGELOG edits.\n\n## Ambiguities I resolved\n- \"Works\" = litnotes whose `pub-author` links to the note; \"edited only\" = `pub-editor` link and no `pub-author` link to the same person.\n- The commands act on the current note, not the whole vault.\n- An existing table is kept and only filled; its spec is not replaced.\n- No saved view used: the built-ins from #330 list via `bib-parent`, not `pub-author`.\n- Branch is `332-author-works-backfill` because I guessed the PR number; it came out as #333. Not renamed, since that would close the PR.\n\n## Testing\n- `tests/sp-author-notes-test.el` (28) and `tests/sp-author-notes-bibtex-test.el` (8) pass on Emacs in a cloud container, with the block writer stubbed. The `:except-prop` match was checked with stubbed vulpea functions only (the query-tables test file cannot load here for missing deps). Not run with real vulpea or in the real vault.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAaYiYrU4FW8BNZKiB",
